Now I have a clear picture of the entire flow. The key insight is:

1. tool_recovery_hint(tool_name, attempt) only takes tool name and attempt number
2. Both build_retry_prompt and build_auto_retry_prompt already have the error message available but don't pass it
3. RecoveryHintTool has the error message (msg) but doesn't pass it to the hint function

The improvement: make tool_recovery_hint error-pattern-aware by accepting an optional error message parameter. This way:
• When edit_file fails with "No such file" → suggest write_file to create it
• When edit_file fails with "old_text not found" → suggest `read_file` (current behavior, but more specific)
• When bash fails with "permission denied" → suggest chmod 
• When bash fails with "command not found" → suggest checking installation
• When write_file fails with "No such file or directory" → suggest `mkdir -p`
• When read_file/list_files fails with "not found" → suggest verifying path
• When search fails with pattern error → suggest simplifying the pattern

